Nephi wrote on 09/24/2003 07:00 PM:
> Well, I beat the odds and actually cranked out a preliminary Pirate
> Patch.

Very cool! Here are a couple of comments:

> A few details and questions:
> 
> Pirates can only be chaotic and human. (No other races seem to be
> seafaring and the idea of a non-chaotic pirate seems rather silly.)

I agree with the chaoticity, but orcs should definitely be able to be
pirates (albeit not very fine ones, perhaps with very low Cha)..I saw
them sailing on a few occasions.

> Deities:
> L:Nereus
> N:Proteus
> C:Poseidon
> 
> Someone suggested these with Proteus and Poseidon reversed, but
> Poseidon is already chaotic for healers.

Don't think classical myth is appropriate for pirates. I'm not sure they
were really very religious, but they sure were supersticious, so perhaps
some of the suggested woodoo (or whatever it was) stuff would fit more?
AFAIR Wiki has some good details no $deities.

> Stat distribution (for source divers)
> /* Str Int Wis Dex Con Cha */
> {   8,  7, 7,  8,  8,  7 },
> {  20, 15, 10, 20, 25, 10 },

Does that mean they have much Con? Why's that?

> What do you think of [skill] distribution?

They should be expert in two-weapon, I would think. Perhaps cut on some
of the other skills. Trident seems funny for eg., but does it REALLY
make sense?

Also, generally for object-renaming: I don't think there's need for
absolute resemblance between things renamed. For pirates there are many
more opportunities like dagger->machete, etc. As long as the stats and
functionality of the objects are appropriate, there won't be any problems?

